@startuml C4 Dynamic - Create/Update Dock
' Using UML sequence style for clarity within C4 docs
skinparam monochrome true
actor "Port Authority Officer" as Officer
participant "SPA (Web UI)" as SPA
participant "API: DocksController" as Ctrl
participant "DockAppService" as App
participant "Dock Aggregate" as Domain
participant "DockRepository" as Repo
participant "DbContext" as Db

== Create Dock ==
Officer -> SPA: Fill form (dock details)
SPA -> Ctrl: POST /api/docks {CreateDockRequest}
Ctrl -> App: CreateDock(request)
App -> Domain: Validate invariants (draft <= depth, unique name, allowed types)
App -> Repo: Add(Dock)
Repo -> Db: SaveChanges()
Db --> Repo: OK
Repo --> App: Dock saved
App --> Ctrl: DockResponse (201)
Ctrl --> SPA: 201 Created + body

== Update Dock ==
Officer -> SPA: Edit dock
SPA -> Ctrl: PUT /api/docks/{id} {UpdateDockRequest}
Ctrl -> App: UpdateDock(id, request)
App -> Repo: GetById(id)
Repo -> Db: Query
Db --> Repo: Dock
App -> Domain: Apply changes + validate
App -> Repo: Update(Dock)
Repo -> Db: SaveChanges()
Db --> Repo: OK
App --> Ctrl: DockResponse (200)
Ctrl --> SPA: 200 OK
@enduml